---
import Section from '@/components/Section.astro';
import portrait from '@/images/me.webp';
import { site } from '@/data/site';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
---

<Section id="about" heading="About" class="py-2xl">
  <div class="gap-lg sm:gap-xl flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
    <Image
      src={portrait}
      alt={`${site.name}, ${site.role.toLowerCase()}`}
      widths={[140, 280, 420]}
      sizes="140px"
      loading="lazy"
      class="border-rule h-[140px] w-[140px] shrink-0 rounded-full border object-cover"
    />

    <div class="prose-measure gap-lg text-md flex flex-col">
      <p>
        I got into software sideways. I started out in technical theater,
        designing lighting and running stage production. Most of that job was
        setup nobody in the audience ever sees. That led to work as a computer
        technician integrating systems and servers, and eventually to writing
        code, which is where I stayed.
      </p>
      <p>
        That habit stuck. Build it carefully so it holds up once people are
        actually using it, and keep the messy parts out of sight. These days
        that mostly means front-end work: interfaces that stay fast and
        accessible, and code the next person can actually read. I do enough
        back-end to ship a feature end to end.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Section>
